// Process launch is an explicit host effect. `executable` and each argument
// are passed as separate values; no shell parses or interpolates them. The
// caller supplies the working directory and complete child environment, so
// no process inherits an implicit CWD or unlisted ambient variables. Child
// environment names use the portable ASCII form [A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*; duplicate
// names, invalid names, and NUL-containing values fail. A null input closes
// stdin immediately; supplied bytes are written and then closed.
// `timeout` is null for no deadline and otherwise nonnegative. A timeout
// terminates and joins the child before returning an ordinary error; effects
// the child already performed are not undone by an Orna rollback. The output
// limit is positive and counts stdout plus stderr; exceeding it terminates the
// child and fails rather than returning truncated output. A nonzero exit is a
// normal result tuple `(exit_status, stdout, stderr)`. Null exit status means
// the host could not provide an exit code. The host policy validates
// executable and working-directory access.
// This effect is unavailable to assertions, read-only watches, presenters,
// and historical evaluation.
pub fn run(
    executable: Str,
    arguments: [Str],
    working_directory: Str,
    environment: [(Str, Str)],
    input: Blob?,
    timeout: Duration?,
    max_output_bytes: Int,
): (Int?, Blob, Blob) = fail(error(
    code: "ORNA-EVAL-UNSUPPORTED",
    message: "std.io.process.run requires its process evaluator binding"
));
